// D15569: a width-generic float intrinsic named as a value takes the width its destination's
// function type names, so an f32 destination reads f32 `sqrt`, equal to `sqrt(x as f32)`.
// The un-annotated face and `return_inferred` pin nothing, so they read the default width by
// the same ruling: an f32 argument widens to f64, so that face prints the f64 root (WRONG).
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/README.md, "Template format".
// @@VALUE@@
sqrt
// @@TYPE@@
(f32) => f32
// @@TEST@@
v(16.0 as f32) == (4.0 as f32)
// @@HIT@@
print(v(2.0 as f32))
// @@MISS@@
print("miss")
// @@WANT@@
1.4142135381698608
